\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cold-start convergence and retrospective evolution of the standardized bridge radius across the four CWRU operating conditions. The blue segment shows the sequential estimate $\tau _{\mathrm  {bridge},k}(t)=\mu _k(t)+z_{\mathrm  {MC}}\sigma _k(t)$ during the prescribed 100-window calibration interval. The red dotted line marks the detected convergence index, and the blue dash-dotted line marks the end of the calibration interval. The gray segment is a retrospective continuation using the remaining known-healthy observations and is not used by the deployed detector. The horizontal orange line indicates the bridge radius computed from the complete healthy residual mean and standard deviation, whereas the horizontal green line indicates the complete-data empirical p98 field-oracle reference.\relax }}{13}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tau-convergence}{{4}{13}{Cold-start convergence and retrospective evolution of the standardized bridge radius across the four CWRU operating conditions. The blue segment shows the sequential estimate $\tau _{\mathrm {bridge},k}(t)=\mu _k(t)+z_{\mathrm {MC}}\sigma _k(t)$ during the prescribed 100-window calibration interval. The red dotted line marks the detected convergence index, and the blue dash-dotted line marks the end of the calibration interval. The gray segment is a retrospective continuation using the remaining known-healthy observations and is not used by the deployed detector. The horizontal orange line indicates the bridge radius computed from the complete healthy residual mean and standard deviation, whereas the horizontal green line indicates the complete-data empirical p98 field-oracle reference.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
